         <listPerson>
            <person sex="1">
               <persName xml:id="n1" xml:lang="ar">البكري, محمد بن محمد ابو الحسن بن محمد بن عبد الرحمان الصديقي </persName>
               <persName corresp="#n1" type="transliterated">al-Bakrī, Muḥammad b. Muḥammad Abū al-Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. ʻAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṣiddīqī </persName>
               <persName type="alt" xml:id="n2" xml:lang="ar">ابو المكارم شمس الدين</persName>
               <persName corresp="#n2" type="transliterated">Abū al-Makārim Šams al-Dīn</persName>
               <persName type="alt" xml:id="n3" xml:lang="ar">القطب البكري</persName>
               <persName corresp="#n3" type="transliterated">al-Quṭb al-Bakrī</persName>
               <persName type="alt" xml:id="n4" xml:lang="ar">البكري الكبير</persName>
               <persName corresp="#n4" type="transliterated">al-Bakrī al-Kabīr</persName>
               <persName type="alt" xml:id="n5" xml:lang="ar">سيدي محمد البكري</persName>
               <persName corresp="#n5" type="transliterated">Sayyidī Muḥammad al-Bakrī</persName>
               <floruit>10th / 16th century (d. 952 / 1545)<note>Egyptian poet, mystic and Šāfiʻī scholar. Author of al-Ḥizb.

The additional names given above are based on al-Ziriklī.

al-Ziriklī notes that Brockelmann mixes his biography with that of his father Abū al-Ḥasan al-Bakrī. The mix-up is repeated in Encyclopaedia of Islam, where the entry on al-Bakrī is written by Brockelmann.</note>
               </floruit>
               <birth evidence="internal" calendar="hijri" when-custom="0930">0930 </birth>
               <death evidence="internal" calendar="hijri" when-custom="0994">0994 </death>
            </person>
